WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.174
Weaponization and delivery are often paired because one describes preparation of a

00:00:04.174 --> 00:00:07.908
harmful capability and the other describes movement toward the target environment.

00:00:07.908 --> 00:00:11.302
In this course, those stages stay high level and defensive.

00:00:11.302 --> 00:00:16.734
The useful defender view is about reducing the chance that suspicious content reaches users or systems,

00:00:16.734 --> 00:00:19.789
and improving the chance that attempted delivery is noticed.

00:00:19.789 --> 00:00:22.844
Email security controls, attachment handling, web filtering, application allowlisting,

00:00:22.844 --> 00:00:26.579
supplier review, safe file handling, and user reporting all matter here.

00:00:26.579 --> 00:00:27.597
So does telemetry.

00:00:27.597 --> 00:00:31.331
If a suspicious file is blocked, a user reports a message,

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:33.368
or an inbound pattern changes suddenly,

00:00:33.368 --> 00:00:36.763
the team should have enough context to investigate without guessing.

00:00:36.763 --> 00:00:39.478
Delivery is also a human and process problem.

00:00:39.478 --> 00:00:42.534
People need an easy way to report suspicious content,

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:47.626
and analysts need a reliable way to connect those reports to logs and control events.

00:00:47.626 --> 00:00:51.020
The goal is not to teach how delivery works offensively.

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:55.094
The goal is to help defenders ask whether inbound paths are governed,

00:00:55.094 --> 00:00:57.131
whether controls are producing usable evidence,

00:00:57.131 --> 00:01:01.883
and whether response teams can connect a suspicious delivery signal to later system behavior.

00:01:01.883 --> 00:01:04.260
Delivery-focused defense should also include workflow clarity.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:09.012
When a user reports suspicious content, the team should know where the report goes,

00:01:09.012 --> 00:01:12.407
how it is enriched, how similar activity is searched for,

00:01:12.407 --> 00:01:16.820
and how results are communicated back to the people who need to act.
